# SHARED repository SECRETS — every repo in repos.env gets these.
#
# 1. Copy:  cp config/secrets.env.example config/secrets.env
# 2. Fill in the real values (the copy is gitignored).
# 3. Sync:  bin/gh-bootstrap.sh --all
#
# A repo adds or overrides any key in its own .github/secrets.env (the repo's
# value wins). Shared secrets for a GitHub ENVIRONMENT would go in
# config/secrets.<environment>.env, overridable by the repo's
# .github/secrets.<environment>.env — none exist today: every deploy secret is
# specific to one repo's deploy target.
#
# GITHUB_TOKEN is provided automatically by Actions — never set it here.

# Anthropic API key used by auto-work-items.yml to describe issues/PRs.
# https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# CLASSIC PAT used by auto-work-items.yml and promote-dev-to-main.yml to write to
# your user Projects (v2) boards, and so the PRs they open trigger PR Checks.
# Scopes: `project` (read/write on Projects v2) and `repo` (create issues/PRs on
# private repos).
#
# It must be classic, not fine-grained: the boards are owned by your personal
# account, and a fine-grained PAT only offers a Projects permission under
# ORGANIZATION permissions — there is no account-level equivalent, so it cannot
# reach a user-owned board at all. The cost is that `repo` cannot be narrowed to
# selected repositories the way a fine-grained token can, so keep the expiry
# short. One token serves every repo.
# https://github.com/settings/tokens
GH_PROJECT_TOKEN=ghp_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
